Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:42:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: Add Apple VXD video decoder
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Apple A9 (S8000/S8003) has a hardware video decoder, "VXD": an
Imagination PowerVR MSVDX core whose MTX microcontroller runs the DEVA
firmware. It has no DART and translates its own accesses through a GART
the host programs. Describe its register window, interrupt and power
domain.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux b4d792c0 (J71t ledger 12.1); generic node
 name in the example, the missing irq.h include added, the firmware file
 location moved out of the binding into the driver.]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../bindings/media/apple,s8000-vxd.yaml       | 57 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 57 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,s8000-vxd.yaml

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,s8000-vxd.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,s8000-vxd.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..6cb5e83f4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/apple,s8000-vxd.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/media/apple,s8000-vxd.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Apple VXD video decoder (Imagination PowerVR MSVDX)
+
+maintainers:
+  - Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
+
+description:
+  The Apple "VXD" block is a multi-standard hardware video decoder, an
+  Imagination PowerVR MSVDX core whose MTX (META) microcontroller runs the
+  DEVA firmware. Apple has used this IP family since the S5L8940X (A4); the
+  S8000/S8003 (A9) reports vxd-version 7 in the Apple device tree. The block
+  has no DART; it translates its own memory accesses through a two-level
+  "GART" that the host programs through the MTX MMU registers.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: apple,s8000-vxd
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  interrupts:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  power-domains:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - interrupts
+  - power-domains
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/apple-aic.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
+
+    soc {
+        #address-cells = <2>;
+        #size-cells = <2>;
+
+        video-codec@207f00000 {
+            compatible = "apple,s8000-vxd";
+            reg = <0x2 0x07f00000 0x0 0x100000>;
+            interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+            interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 157 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+            power-domains = <&ps_vdec>;
+        };
+    };
